    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-09T09:18:28+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-09T09:18:28+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-08T23:48:28Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-08T23:48:28Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred south of WA extends a ridge across the south of SA. The main high centre will move eastwards during the week to be centred to the east of SA on Friday. A trough over the interior of WA will remain stationary for most of the week and may extend into the far west of SA at times. Another low pressure trough will approach from the west on Saturday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-09T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-10T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-08T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-09T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. High chance of showers in the far west, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Coober Pedy. Winds east to southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h decreasing to 20 to 30 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures between 16 and 20.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:30am to 3:20pm, UV Index predicted to reach 7 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-10T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-11T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-09T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-10T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers in the far west, most likely in the early morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far west. Winds easterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 22.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-11T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-12T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-10T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-11T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the morning. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-12T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-13T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-11T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-12T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far west in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm south of Coober Pedy in the evening. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
